0. THE CLAIM

If the paper proofs in A1–A5 are sound, and the system is finite and deterministic, then the TLA+ model-check is mechanical. This document is the attempt to make that claim testable.

The TLA+ modules below are not skeletons. They are complete enough to run. What remains is (a) concrete constant values for a deployment, (b) a .cfg file, (c) a TLC run.

If TLC finds nothing, the theorem is machine-checked.
If TLC finds a counterexample, the paper proof was wrong.
Either outcome is informative.

