MODULE 3 — STT1024_A3_Plans.tla

```tla
-------------------------- MODULE STT1024_A3_Plans --------------------------
EXTENDS Naturals, FiniteSets, Sequences,
        STT1024_A4_State,
        STT1024_A2_Actions

CONSTANTS
    PlanIDs,        \* Finite plan identifier set
    K,              \* Max plan length (Nat)
    Dinvoke         \* Max invocation depth (Nat)

ASSUME FinitePlanIDs == IsFiniteSet(PlanIDs)
ASSUME KPos          == K \in Nat /\ K > 0
ASSUME DInvokePos    == Dinvoke \in Nat /\ Dinvoke > 0

\* Step kinds (A3 §2.2)
StepKind == {"action", "plan", "conditional"}

\* Step schema — simplified to bound model-checking state space.
\* Each step carries a kind, a target ID, and a depth tag.
Step == [
    kind   : StepKind,
    target : ActionIDs \cup PlanIDs,
    depth  : 0..Dinvoke
]

\* Bounded-step predicate (A3 §2.3)
StepBounded(step) ==
    \/ step.kind = "action"
    \/ /\ step.kind = "plan"
       /\ step.depth < Dinvoke
    \/ /\ step.kind = "conditional"
       /\ step.depth <= Dinvoke

\* Plan schema (A3 §2.1)
Plan == [
    id           : PlanIDs,
    precondition : PredicateIDs,
    steps        : Seq(Step),
    postcondition: PredicateIDs,
    budget_cycles: Nat,
    version      : Nat
]

\* Bounded plan predicate (A3 §2.3, B3)
BoundedPlan(p) ==
    /\ Len(p.steps) <= K
    /\ \A i \in DOMAIN p.steps : StepBounded(p.steps[i])

\* The plan library.
P == { p \in Plan : BoundedPlan(p) }

\* A3 obligation: every plan in P is bounded.
THEOREM A3_BoundedPlans ==
    \A p \in P : BoundedPlan(p)

=============================================================================
```

