MODULE 6 — STT1024_Core.tla

```tla
--------------------------- MODULE STT1024_Core -----------------------------
EXTENDS Naturals, FiniteSets, Sequences,
        STT1024_A1_FSM,
        STT1024_A2_Actions,
        STT1024_A3_Plans,
        STT1024_A4_State,
        STT1024_A5_Verify

\* The core soundness theorem: every sub-spec obligation holds.
THEOREM CoreSoundness ==
    /\ STT1024_A1_FSM!Determinism
    /\ STT1024_A1_FSM!StructurallySafe
    /\ STT1024_A3_Plans!A3_BoundedPlans
    /\ STT1024_A5_Verify!A5_InvariantPreservation

\* The Verifiable Agency Theorem (paper proof, now stated formally).
\*
\* The behavior set B is the set of all finite action sequences the agent can
\* produce. Under the finite-state, finite-action, finite-plan, bounded-budget
\* assumptions of A1–A5, B is finite, constructible, and envelope-compliant.
\*
\* A full formalization of B requires concretizing "trace". In this module,
\* B is defined structurally: for any trace of length ≤ T_AET, its action
\* projection belongs to a finite set.

\* Trace: a finite sequence of (mode, cost) pairs.
Trace == {
    t \in Seq(M_all \X Nat) :
        /\ Len(t) <= T_AET
        /\ t[1][1] = "IDLE"                      \* starts at IDLE
        /\ t[Len(t)][1] \in {"POWER_DOWN"}
                                                  \cup M_halt \cup M_error
}

\* Behavior set: action projections of all traces.
\* (In this structural encoding, "action" is abstracted to the FSM mode.)
BehaviorSet ==
    { [i \in 1..Len(t) |-> t[i][1]] : t \in Trace }

\* The theorem.
THEOREM VerifiableAgency ==
    /\ IsFiniteSet(BehaviorSet)
    \* Envelope compliance is established by A5's invariant preservation
    \* theorem (see STT1024_A5_Verify!A5_InvariantPreservation).

=============================================================================
```

